Connect technical decisions with affected people, rights, evidence, and continuing work (@mine-communities: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Community-Engagement-and-Development-Handbook.lingua#r_2RSVNSY8QJJ3XF6YGJ7TBADM89", #source "../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM", #source "../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Products-specifications-custody-and-refining-interfaces.lingua#r_4WQ464KMKXECT0MF2ASW2H6D4G") { r_222K818VT9AFN33GJFZ08QB4P0
**Read:** [Community engagement and development — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Community-Engagement-and-Development-Handbook.lingua#r_2RSVNSY8QJJ3XF6YGJ7TBADM89), the whole handbook and complete chosen case studies; [Water stewardship — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM), the full relevant stewardship and affected-use context; [Mine closure — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN), the complete future-use and continuing-responsibility discussions.

A mine changes land and water use, movement, livelihoods, work, local infrastructure, and the distribution of benefits and burdens. These relationships begin before extraction and continue through closure. Technical evidence matters, but agreement about a physical model is not automatically agreement about an acceptable outcome or decision process.

Identify the actual people and organizations affected, their differing knowledge, uses, authority, and responsibilities, and how these change over time. Distinguish legal rights/requirements, engineering recommendations, voluntary standards, contracts, and community expectations by their own primary evidence. Preserve disagreement and unavailable evidence rather than presenting a consultation summary as universal consent.

Connect engagement with specific design choices and observations: water supply/quality, access, dust/noise, work conditions, landforms, emergency response, and future use. Information should be understandable, accessible, timely, and connected with a way for concerns and new evidence to change decisions. Do not turn a learning case into publication of private consultation or health information.

**Work:** reconstruct one complete public case from both technical and affected-party evidence where available. Trace a disputed claim to its observation/model and a disputed decision to its stated authority and values. Compare an alternative design through physical consequences and continuing work. Explain whose evidence remains absent and which observations or shared inquiry would most improve the account.

**Continue:** [Define the product and evidence transferred between mine, processor, transporter, and refiner](Products-specifications-custody-and-refining-interfaces.lingua#r_4WQ464KMKXECT0MF2ASW2H6D4G).

